  "content": {
    "id": "p50-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "If the graph of $y=k(x+2)(x-4)$ passes through the point $(2,16)$, determine the value of $k$ using substitution, and hence the coordinates of the turning point for this parabola.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$k=-2$; turning point $(1,18)$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}16&=k(2+2)(2-4)\\\\16&=-8k\\\\k&=-2\\end{align*}$$\nThe turning point lies halfway between the $x$-intercepts $-2$ and $4$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{-2+4}{2}\\\\x&=1\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute $x=1$ into $y=-2(x+2)(x-4)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=-2(1+2)(1-4)\\\\y&=18\\end{align*}$$\nTurning point: $(1,18)$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 62
  },
